   "id": "u08-l01",
   "title": "Skal and vil with an infinitive",
   "pages": [
    43
   ],
   "taughtInClass": true,
   "tip": "Skal + infinitive is for appointments and plans; vil + infinitive is for wishes and decisions. After skal/vil the infinitive has no \"at\".\nWord order: Subject – skal/vil – infinitive. In questions the modal comes first: Skal du lære russisk?\nExample: Hun skal have gæster i weekenden. (More modal verbs: see unit 7, p.41.)",
